(-2 Delta X)|/2<=1, while the exact residual envelope gives operator norm at most V_bar<1.","Banach contraction yields a unique bounded H; |H-1| and |H_X| are at most q_bar, and the tail norm tends to zero so H tends to 1.","The branches and kernel are holomorphic for |z|<9/8 and the uniformly convergent Neumann series makes the normalized solution holomorphic there."],"statement":"The self-contained Volterra proof fixes one and only one solution in the bounded-H class with u/u0 tending to 1; without that limit the second-order equation retains scalar freedom.","uniqueness_class":"bounded H=exp(X)*p_A^(1/2)*u with lim H=1"},{"endpoint_same_backend_overlap":true,"id":"rawc.p4.volterra.control.endpoint_value_derivative_correction_enclosures_finite","passed":true,"rectangle_enlargement":"each real and imaginary component is enlarged by the full complex absolute-error radius; correlations are discarded conservatively","statement":"At Q+=4, |u-u0|<=|u0|q_bar and |u'-u0'|<=q_bar(|u0'|+|p_A*u0|); adding each disk radius to both rectangular components is conservative and gives finite outward endpoint enclosures."}],"convention_provenance":{"path":"cpt_temporal_folded_susy/RAW_C_NONREAL_WEYL_PROXY_INPUTS.json","role":"pins only the raw-C nonreal coefficient convention; no proxy result is used as theorem evidence","sha256":"a4ddbe579cf3f39704e043cd3ecbe174708e8df199f0e4d1abe3a359ecf176ce"},"declared_conventions":{"Q_domain":"Q>=4 along the real half-line","Q_plus":"4","analytic_eta_bar":"1/336","coefficient":"A(Q,z)=36*pi^4*exp(2Q)+6*pi^2*z*exp(3Q/2)=36*pi^4*exp(2Q)*(1+delta(Q,z))","contraction_majorant":"V_bar=R_bar/(6*9*49*(1-eta_bar))","execution":"exact SymPy identities and monotone half-line majorants, followed only by outward python-flint acb/arb evaluation of fixed-box Q=4 constants and endpoint rectangles; no ODE, quadrature, root solver, finite-difference, or sampling grid","fixed_point_error_majorant":"q_bar=V_bar/(1-V_bar)","holomorphy_neighborhood":"open disk |z|<